      "provenance": {
        "notes": "NAME CLASH: common jasmine (Jasminum officinale, row 73), winter jasmine, the pot 'jazmin chino' (J. polyanthum) and false jasmine (Trachelospermum, row 200) are different plants; the first four are Jasminum with different hardiness. Tender: RHS H2 (1 to 5 C), grow indoors or in a heated greenhouse in bright light with shade from hot sun, water sparingly in winter. The RHS jasmine growing guide does not mention sambac (its 13 C minimum is for J. polyanthum), so no temperature range is stored. Size: the RHS species page says up to 2.5 to 4 m by 0.5 to 1 m; NC State's genus page says pot plants usually stay at 4 to 5 ft. Toxicity: the ASPCA entry is for Jasminum species in general (non-toxic to dogs and cats), so it is a genus-level reading for this species (from_knowledge_verify); no page names J. sambac. RHS and NC State are silent on toxicity."
      },
